FINAL ORDER OF THE 9 TECHNIQUES:
1. Backup Everything - copy entire root folder with " ORIGINAL" suffix
2. Environment Differences - Python version, packages, paths, .env, case sensitivity
3. 30-Second Obvious Checklist - saved file? restarted server? typo? right branch?
4. Stack Trace Reading - read from bottom up, find where bad data entered
5. Binary Search Debugging - comment out half, narrow to exact line
6. Debugger Commands (pdb) - breakpoint(), inspect variables, step through
7. Rubber Duck Debugging - Claude reads every file systematically
8. Git Troubleshooting - git diff, git bisect, git stash
9. Minimal Reproducible Example - strip code to smallest version that breaks

