================================================================================
QUESTIONING FRAMEWORK
================================================================================

USER: Keep API troubleshooting; what is the questioning framework? Show me both,
one at a time in high school language for adults.

CLAUDE: Explained Questioning Framework in plain language:

The questioning framework is a set of "check yourself" questions organized into
4 groups. Each group matches a stage of debugging:

GROUP 1 - "What's broken?" (before you start searching)
- What is the exact error message?
- What was I trying to do?
- What should have happened instead?
- Can I make it break again on purpose?
- What exact steps caused the error?

GROUP 2 - "Why is it broken?" (after you found the bug)
- Which specific part is actually failing?
- What am I assuming that might be wrong?
- Am I looking at the right thing?

GROUP 3 - "How do I fix it?" (when creating a solution)
- What are 3 different ways I could solve this?
- Which solution fixes the root cause, not just the symptom?
- What could go wrong with each approach?
- How will I know if the solution actually worked?
- What would prevent this from happening again?

GROUP 4 - "Did it actually work?" (after applying the fix)
- Did the fix solve the original problem?
- Did anything else break?
- Does it work every time, not just once?

