================================================================================
SUBAGENT DEFINITIONS SUMMARY
================================================================================

CP1BUGSEARCH (.claude/agents/cp1-bug-search.md)
  Model: opus | Color: green
  Purpose: Find bugs using 9 ordered techniques
  Wiki: standards/coding_process_step01_bug_search.md
  Process:
    1. Answer Group 1 questioning framework questions
    2. Backup Everything (Technique 1)
    3. Run Techniques 2-9 in order, stop at first bug
    4. Answer Group 2 questioning framework questions
    5. If API bug -> launch CP1API first
    6. Hand off to CP2BUGFIX

CP1API (.claude/agents/cp1-api.md)
  Model: opus | Color: orange
  Purpose: Diagnose API communication failures (6 phases)
  Wiki: standards/coding_process_step01_API.md
  Process:
    Phase 1: Is the other program alive? (process, port, HTTP, endpoint)
    Phase 2: Right format? (JSON vs Form Data vs URL Encoded)
    Phase 3: Right data? (log everything, check payload)
    Phase 4: Configs in sync? (discover, analyze, compare)
    Phase 5: Server-side error? (logs, clues, minimal payload)
    Phase 6: Auth and headers?
  Reports back to CP1BUGSEARCH (does NOT fix anything)

CP2BUGFIX (.claude/agents/cp2-bug-fix.md)
  Model: opus | Color: yellow
  Purpose: Fix the bug found by CP1
  Wiki: standards/coding_process_step02_bug_fix.md
  Process:
    Step 1: Read the wiki
    Step 2: Check launch file for logging console (create if missing)
    Step 3: Determine bug source (Technique 2/3 vs 4-9)
      - If 2/3: fix directly -> CP3SIM
      - If 4-9: continue to Step 4
    Step 4: Check [root folder]_Fix_LOG.md (create if missing)
    Step 5: Answer Group 3 questions, create solution NOT in the log
    Step 6: Add solution to the log
    Step 7: Implement the solution
    Step 8: Launch CP3SIM
  Rules: NO SHORTCUTS. NO WORKAROUNDS. NO DUMMIES. NO PLACEHOLDERS.
         NO STUBS. NO NUBS.

CP3SIM (.claude/agents/cp3-simulation.md)
  Model: opus | Color: red
  Purpose: Simulate the app to verify the fix worked
  Wiki: standards/coding_process_step03_bug_fix_simulation.md
  Process:
    Step 1: Read the wiki
    Step 2: Watch the logging console
    Step 3: Launch the app
    Step 4: Simulate the original error, answer Group 4 questions
    Step 5: Evaluate:
      - SAME ERROR -> undo fix, add FAIL to log, back to CP2
      - DIFFERENT ERROR -> keep fix, back to CP1 for new bug
      - NO ERROR -> mark PASS, done

================================================================================
THE LOOP (visual)
================================================================================

CP1 finds bug
  -> CP2 checks for logging console in launch file (adds if missing)
  -> CP2 checks if bug is from Technique 2 or 3
      -> Yes? Fix directly -> CP3SIM
      -> No? Continue below
  -> CP2 checks for [root folder]_Fix_LOG.md (creates if missing)
  -> CP2 creates solution NOT already in the log
     (no shortcuts, no workarounds, no dummies, no placeholders, no stubs, no nubs)
  -> CP2 adds new solution to the log
  -> CP2 implements solution
  -> CP3 launches app, watches console for errors, simulates error
      -> Same error? Undo fix -> add failed attempt to log -> back to CP2 (new solution)
      -> Different error? -> back to CP1 (new bug search)
      -> No error? Done.

